  "findings": [
    "SequenceDiagram.activate overwrites one pending CREATE; addMessage validates, attaches and clears. Message.compatibleForCreate excludes source and self; MessageExo accepts its sole real participant. The new event-index helper follows these parser ownership rules, and no serialized field was added. LifeLine.setCreate and LivingSpace.goCreate independently overwrite their origins.",
    "NEW REGRESSION: all four ind78_outgoing_left/right legacy/teoz cases match Java before but panic after at crates/rustuml-render/src/sequence.rs:14287:81. The helper now attaches outgoing MessageExo CREATE events; create_msg_idx feeds created_inline/is_create_msg, and the ordinary creation endpoint code unwraps id_to_idx[msg.to], which is '[' or ']'. Valid Java input reaches this panic. Incoming exo cases remain whole failures.",
    "The Java render consumers are distinct: DrawableSetInitializer.prepareMessageExo dispatches Step1MessageExo, which creates MessageExoArrow without Step1Message.createArrowCreate; Teoz CommunicationExoTile has no CommunicationTile goCreate/head branch. Accepting an exo CREATE attachment does not authorize ordinary participant-target creation geometry. A null check alone would not establish semantic parity.",
    "Fresh triple/interleaved overwrite, lowered compatible return, intervening activation/deactivation, autonumber and dangling participant/actor/queue CREATE controls exercise both engines. Raw event counts, head/tail groups where present, total shapes and exact label multiplicities are preserved. In prior double-pending legacy Roe labels fall 3 to Java 2; in maker pending_same actor ellipses/labels fall 4 to Java 3 while all three raw CREATEs remain. Group/box controls retain whole failures and are not waived.",
    "Eight fresh Java command-error references (source, self, neither receiver, incompatible lowered return in both engines) change from successful Rust rendering to real parser exit1; all valid fresh AST/ASCII commands remain exit0. No Java-valid fresh source becomes a parse rejection. Four valid SVG commands instead panic, which refutes any broader no-new-valid-input-error claim."
  ],
